@CreatorPlatform.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:0

GET {{CreatorPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/weatherforecast/
Accept: application/json

###

### Task 5 — Payout administration manual verification
### Grant the platform_admin role first (run once against the dev DB, then log the admin user in via the
### normal /auth/login flow so the session cookie picks up the role on next request):
###   INSERT INTO auth.user_roles ("UserId","RoleId","CreatedAt") VALUES (<admin-user-id>, 2, now());

### 1. List BankTransfer creators with a payable balance (defaults to Payouts:MinPayoutCents = 5000)
GET {{CreatorPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/api/admin/payouts/balances?minCents=5000&limit=100
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Create a payout for a creator (creatorPublicId from the balances list above)
POST {{CreatorPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/api/admin/payouts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "creatorPublicId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "amountCents": 10000,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "note": "October payout"
}

###

### 3. Concurrency check (acceptance criterion #3): fire this same request twice in quick succession
### (e.g. two terminals running `curl -X POST .../api/admin/payouts -d '{...}'` at the same time) —
### the pg_advisory_xact_lock serializes them, so exactly one succeeds (201) and the other gets a 409
### ConflictException ("Creator's balance is insufficient for this payout.").

### 4. Mark the payout paid (publicId from step 2's response)
POST {{CreatorPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/api/admin/payouts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/mark-paid
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bankReference": "REF-2026-001"
}

###

### 5. Mark a payout failed instead (books a compensating Adjustment that restores the creator's balance)
POST {{CreatorPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/api/admin/payouts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/mark-failed
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": "Wrong IBAN, resubmitting next cycle"
}

###

### 6. Creator-facing: balance summary (null data for StripeConnect-mode creators)
GET {{CreatorPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/api/creators/acme/payouts/summary
Accept: application/json

###

### 7. Creator-facing: payout history (last 50, newest first)
GET {{CreatorPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/api/creators/acme/payouts
Accept: application/json

###

### 8. Creator-facing: save IBAN — acceptance criterion #4: the response's MaskedIban never contains
### the full number, only "XX00 **** **** 6819" style
PUT {{CreatorPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/api/creators/acme/payout-profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountHolderName": "Acme Doo",
  "iban": "GB29NWBK60161331926819",
  "bankCountryCode": "GB"
}

###

### 9. Creator-facing: read back the payout profile — confirm only the masked IBAN comes back
GET {{CreatorPlatform.Api_HostAddress}}/api/creators/acme/payout-profile
Accept: application/json

###
